 "intro": "Numantia, a Celtiberian hill town in northern Spain, 134-133 BC. It has defeated several Roman armies over twenty years. You are Publius Cornelius Scipio Aemilianus, conqueror of Carthage, with about 60,000 men.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s account, Scipio restored discipline, then ringed Numantia with a wall nine kilometres long with towers and seven camps, and blocked the Douro with a boom of spiked timbers. When the noble Rhetogenes escaped to seek help, Scipio rode to Lutia and cut off the hands of 400 young men who had promised aid. After eight months of starvation, many Numantines killed themselves and the rest surrendered; the town was destroyed. The siege works can still be traced today. The other choices are what-ifs.",
